WEBVTT

NOTE Actual full-workspace tutorial recording. Prepared starter QA account; five later phases explicitly opened. No earned passes, AI, execution, edits or submissions. Normal speed; no added holds.

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.600
1 of 6. Implement the agreed contracts
Open Code and use Files to inspect the supplied project. Work in the editable files for this task, using the contracts and brief to guide your changes. Watch the save status as you edit.

2
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:12.680
2 of 6. Run the tests
Choose Run tests when you are ready to check your work. Read the actual output and failures. If execution is unavailable, it provides no successful result; keep that limitation visible.

3
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:18.720
3 of 6. Inspect the app preview
App preview shows the app when a supported runtime is available. Use the preview’s run control to start it yourself. An idle, failed or unavailable preview is not evidence that the app works.

4
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:24.520
4 of 6. Keep the brief close
Show brief to revisit the task and review criteria. Show mentor opens optional guidance. You can hide either panel to make space; your work and conversations stay in their own phase.

5
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:30.520
5 of 6. Submit the saved implementation
Submit your saved version for review. Open its feedback and exact submitted files, revise the identified behavior, then run and submit again as needed. Running tests alone does not pass the phase.

6
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:36.080
6 of 6. Return whenever you need help
Replay tutorial brings these steps back. Optional phase guide opens the lessons. In the workspace mentor, Guided offers hints. Agentic proposes changes: compare them, explain this exact version in your own words, then choose Apply only if your explanation is accepted. A changed proposal needs a new explanation.
